  "title": "Colleen J NDE 6624",
  "date": "1975",
  "content": "I have no direct recall of the death during the surgery, but afterwards while recovering in the hospital ward I was haunted by an image and memory that I tried to capture in a drawing with color crayons. I tried to draw a tunnel of light that was colorful. I knew with certainty that I could not take my body through the tunnel. I called the ‘place’ I had experience ‘home’ and was homesick for the next twenty years. Even though I was very young, I remember very clearly looking at my hands and feeling that my body was strange to me, compared to the expanded peace and being awake that I felt myself to be. When it was time to be taken home after lengthy recovery. I recall my mother driving us to our house and feeling sad that this house was not my real home. I was left with deep questions, a passion for seeking wisdom and truth. I was a very shy introverted child. Intuitive skills surfaced at about the age of seven and have remained a source of strength and guidance my entire life. My homesickness turned into suicidal feelings at thirteen, but the same presence of ‘home’ comforted me and I dedicated my life to the pursuit of wisdom. The homesick longing eventually lifted in my twenties when I was able to use my intuition to feel and know that ‘home’ was not some other place, but was right here right now, like another radio station away. This realization and many subsequent realizations have left me as a deeply content, happy and spiritually awake person.",
